// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`@zeus-web/ai metadata > matches the AI markdown guide snapshot 1`] = `
"# Zeus Web AI Guide

This file is generated from \`@zeus-web/ai\` metadata.

## Recommended workflow

- Run \`zweb init\` before adding registry-backed styled components.
- Run \`zweb add <component>\` to copy the selected registry source into the user project.
- Import styled components from the copied local path, usually \`@/components/ui/<component>\`.
- Use \`@zeus-web/ui\` for package-owned styled native Web Components.
- Use per-component packages such as \`@zeus-web/button/react\` when building advanced primitive-based design systems.

## Themes

- \`default\`
- \`slate\`
- \`zinc\`
- \`neutral\`
- \`stone\`

## Icons

Package: \`@zeus-web/icons\`
Install: \`pnpm add @zeus-web/icons\`
React: \`import { IconCheck, IconX } from '@zeus-web/icons/react'\`
Vue: \`import { IconCheck, IconX } from '@zeus-web/icons/vue'\`
Web Component: \`import '@zeus-web/icons/wc'\`
Raw SVG: \`import checkIcon from '@zeus-web/icons/svg/check.svg'\`

Recommended icons:
- \`check\`
- \`x\`
- \`plus\`
- \`minus\`
- \`chevron-down\`
- \`chevron-up\`
- \`chevron-left\`
- \`chevron-right\`
- \`search\`
- \`menu\`
- \`settings\`
- \`user\`
- \`copy\`
- \`external-link\`
- \`info\`
- \`alert-triangle\`
- \`circle-check\`
- \`circle-x\`
- \`loader\`
- \`sun\`
- \`moon\`
- \`eye\`
- \`eye-off\`
- \`trash\`

Icon AI do:
- Use @zeus-web/icons/react for React examples.
- Use @zeus-web/icons/vue for Vue examples.
- Use @zeus-web/icons/wc when showing native Web Component usage.
- Use aria-hidden for decorative icons.
- Provide an accessible label on the parent control when an icon-only button is used.
- Prefer currentColor icons so color follows text/theme tokens.

Icon AI do not:
- Do not inline random SVG markup when an icon exists in @zeus-web/icons.
- Do not use icons as the only accessible name.
- Do not hardcode width/height when size can be controlled with className or CSS.
- Do not import React icons in Vue examples or Vue icons in React examples.

## Global AI rules: do

- Use Zeus Web registry components for app-level React and Vue code when a registry template exists.
- Use --zeus-* semantic variables inside registry-installed source components.
- Respect zeus-ui.json aliases when generating local imports.
- Use \`zweb add <component>\` for registry-backed components.
- Use \`zweb init --style <theme>\` to set up registry CSS variables.

## Global AI rules: do not

- Do not hand-write Web Component registration code.
- Do not import generated app components from @zeus-web/registry/default/* at runtime.
- Do not style only the custom element host when the primitive exposes internal data-slot or part selectors.
- Do not assume Shadow DOM; current MVP registry styling targets light DOM internals.
- Do not use non-semantic hard-coded colors when theme tokens are available.

# Components

## button

Styled button component built on the zw-button primitive.

Add command: \`zweb add button\`
Styled import: \`import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button'\`
Install command: \`pnpm add @zeus-web/button\`
Primitive React import: \`import { Button } from '@zeus-web/button/react'\`
Web Component import: \`import '@zeus-web/button/wc/auto'\`

### Props

- \`variant\` (\`ButtonVariant\`): Visual style variant.. Values: default, primary, secondary, outline, ghost, danger. Default: default.
- \`size\` (\`ButtonSize\`): Button size.. Values: sm, md, lg, icon. Default: md.
- \`disabled\` (\`boolean\`): Disables user interaction..
- \`loading\` (\`boolean\`): Marks the button as loading and prevents press handling..
- \`ariaLabel\` (\`string\`): Accessible label for icon-only buttons..

### Events

- \`press\` / React \`onPress\`: Emitted when the button is clicked and not disabled.. Detail: nativeEvent: MouseEvent

### Slots

- \`default\`: Button label content.
- \`prefix\`: Content before the label.
- \`suffix\`: Content after the label.

### Styling

Tailwind: yes

Theme tokens:
- bg-primary
- text-primary-foreground
- border-input
- ring-ring

Internal selectors:
- [&_[data-slot=button]]
- [&_[data-slot=button-prefix]]
- [&_[data-slot=button-suffix]]

### AI do

- Use Button for actions.
- Use variant="outline" for secondary actions.
- Use size="icon" only for icon-only buttons.

### AI do not

- Do not add asChild; the current registry Button does not implement asChild.
- Do not attach click handlers to internal button selectors manually.

### React styled usage

\`\`\`tsx
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button'

export function Example() {
  return <Button variant="primary">Save</Button>
}
\`\`\`

---

## input

Styled text input component built on the zw-input primitive.

Add command: \`zweb add input\`
Styled import: \`import { Input } from '@/components/ui/input'\`
Install command: \`pnpm add @zeus-web/input\`
Primitive React import: \`import { Input } from '@zeus-web/input/react'\`
Web Component import: \`import '@zeus-web/input/wc/auto'\`

### Props

- \`value\` (\`string\`): Controlled input value..
- \`defaultValue\` (\`string\`): Initial uncontrolled value..
- \`type\` (\`InputType\`): Native input type.. Values: text, email, password, search, tel, url, number. Default: text.
- \`placeholder\` (\`string\`): Placeholder text..
- \`disabled\` (\`boolean\`): Disables input interaction..
- \`id\` (\`string\`): Native input id attribute..
- \`autocomplete\` (\`string\`): Native input autocomplete attribute..
- \`ariaLabel\` (\`string\`): Accessible label for unlabeled inputs..
- \`ariaDescribedby\` (\`string\`): ID reference for additional accessible description..
- \`ariaErrormessage\` (\`string\`): ID reference for accessible error message..

### Events

- \`value-change\` / React \`onValueChange\`: Emitted when the input value changes.. Detail: value: string, nativeEvent: Event

### Slots

- \`prefix\`: Content before the native input.
- \`suffix\`: Content after the native input.

### Styling

Tailwind: yes

Theme tokens:
- border-input
- ring-ring
- text-muted-foreground

Internal selectors:
- [&_[part=root]]
- [&_[data-slot=input]]

### AI do

- Use Input for text-like form fields.
- Use onValueChange when the user wants Zeus custom events.

### AI do not

- Do not style only the host for placeholder or disabled states.
- Do not assume the native input is the custom element itself.

### React styled usage

\`\`\`tsx
import { Input } from '@/components/ui/input'

export function Example() {
  return <Input placeholder="Email" type="email" />
}
\`\`\`

---

## checkbox

Styled checkbox component built on the zw-checkbox primitive.

Add command: \`zweb add checkbox\`
Styled import: \`import { Checkbox } from '@/components/ui/checkbox'\`
Install command: \`pnpm add @zeus-web/checkbox\`
Primitive React import: \`import { Checkbox } from '@zeus-web/checkbox/react'\`
Web Component import: \`import '@zeus-web/checkbox/wc/auto'\`

### Props

- \`checked\` (\`boolean\`): Controlled checked state..
- \`defaultChecked\` (\`boolean\`): Initial checked state..
- \`indeterminate\` (\`boolean\`): Mixed state..
- \`size\` (\`CheckboxSize\`): Checkbox size.. Values: sm, md, lg. Default: md.
- \`required\` (\`boolean\`): Marks the checkbox as required..
- \`ariaLabel\` (\`string\`): Accessible label for unlabeled checkboxes..
- \`ariaDescribedby\` (\`string\`): ID reference for additional accessible description..

### Events

- \`checked-change\` / React \`onCheckedChange\`: Emitted when checked state changes.. Detail: checked: boolean, nativeEvent: Event
- \`focus-change\` / React \`onFocusChange\`: Emitted when focus state changes.. Detail: focused: boolean, nativeEvent: FocusEvent

### Slots

- \`default\`: Label content.
- \`indicator\`: Custom indicator content.

### Styling

Tailwind: yes

Theme tokens:
- bg-primary
- text-primary-foreground
- ring-ring

Internal selectors:
- [&_[data-slot=checkbox-control]]
- [&_[data-slot=checkbox-indicator]]

### AI do

- Use Checkbox for boolean form choices.
- Use indeterminate for mixed state.

### AI do not

- Do not render a separate native input next to Checkbox.
- Do not manually manage aria-checked when using the primitive props.

### React styled usage

\`\`\`tsx
import { Checkbox } from '@/components/ui/checkbox'

export function Example() {
  return <Checkbox>Accept terms</Checkbox>
}
\`\`\`

