## radio-group

Styled radio group component built on zw-radio-group primitives.

Add command: \`zweb add radio-group\`
Styled import: \`import { RadioGroup, RadioGroupItem } from '@/components/ui/radio-group'\`
Install command: \`pnpm add @zeus-web/radio-group\`
Primitive React import: \`import { RadioGroup, RadioGroupItem } from '@zeus-web/radio-group/react'\`
Web Component import: \`import '@zeus-web/radio-group/wc/auto'\`

### Props

- \`value\` (\`string\`): Controlled selected value..
- \`defaultValue\` (\`string\`): Initial selected value..
- \`name\` (\`string\`): Native radio group name..
- \`orientation\` (\`RadioGroupOrientation\`): Layout orientation.. Values: horizontal, vertical. Default: vertical.
- \`required\` (\`boolean\`): Marks the group as required..

### Events

- \`value-change\` / React \`onValueChange\`: Emitted when selected value changes.. Detail: value: string, nativeEvent: Event

### Slots

- \`default\`: RadioGroupItem children.

### Styling

Tailwind: yes

Theme tokens:
- text-primary
- ring-ring

Internal selectors:
- [data-slot=radio-group-control]
- [data-slot=radio-group-label]

### AI do

- Use RadioGroup for one-of-many choices.
- Keep RadioGroupItem values unique.

### AI do not

- Do not use Checkbox when only one option can be selected.

### React styled usage

\`\`\`tsx
import { RadioGroup, RadioGroupItem } from '@/components/ui/radio-group'

export function Example() {
  return (
    <RadioGroup defaultValue="email">
      <RadioGroupItem value="email">Email</RadioGroupItem>
      <RadioGroupItem value="sms">SMS</RadioGroupItem>
    </RadioGroup>
  )
}
